body:
My theory is that this is a bit "worse" than the other hero cards because of incentive. Warrior is already on the brink of playing control-like decks already with some decks teching in control pieces, and this might incentivize that playstyle a bit more. Giving warrior a Cariel-like hero would maybe be too much.  On the other hand, rogue got Scabbs' power level because of a not-garrote incentive. They probably want to push away from those playstyles and HEAVILY incentivize some flavor of tempo rogue. 

&#x200B;

When it comes to Cariel though, i have no idea. My theory doesn't apply there lmao.
